Aerogel, for the link under the cursor.

"Open link in Aerogel tab", directly under "Open link in incognito window",
because it answers the neighbouring question: that row is "not my usual self,
and leave no local trace", this one is "not my usual self, and I still want my
history". Opening a link into a jar is the case the feature exists for - the
app-menu entry that landed first gives you an empty jar and makes you navigate
into it by hand.

Split out of aerium-aerogel.patch rather than folded into it. That patch
creates chrome/browser/ui/aerium/aerogel.{h,cc} whole; this one only calls into
them, and render_view_context_menu.cc is six thousand lines with strict item
ordering, so keeping the two apart means a rebase that goes wrong here does not
put the mechanism at risk.

Not routed through OpenURLWithExtraHeaders like the rows around it, because a
jar is not a WindowOpenDisposition. The tab has to be built around a
SiteInstance whose storage partition is already fixed, which is what
aerogel::OpenInNewJar does and what a disposition cannot express.

GetBrowser() returns a BrowserWindowInterface here, so the Browser* comes from
GetBrowserForMigrationOnly() - the same route this file already uses twice,
with the same null check. OpenInNewJar tolerates a null browser anyway.

IsCommandIdEnabled needs no separate-profile check, unlike the incognito row
beside it: a jar is an ordinary tab in the window you are already in, so the
only requirement is somewhere to put it.

Generated against, and verified against, a tree carrying the full ungoogled and
Aerium series in order - 21 patches, none failing - applied with GNU patch as
the build applies it.

